<programme start="20261021130000 +0000" stop="20261021140000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Build That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Medals &amp; Marinas</sub-title><desc lang="en">Paying tribute to the brave, gravity-defying design of the U.S. National Medal of Honor Museum; traveling to Singapore for a look at a leaning tower of gambling, then exploring a New York City office building that lets the sun shine through.</desc><category lang="en">Instructional</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19223615_b_v12_aa.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021140000 +0000" stop="20261021150000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Build That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Shipyards &amp; Slender Builds</sub-title><desc lang="en">A 284ft wooden skyscraper built from 1,200 bespoke pieces tests fire safety limits in Milwaukee; a decaying Amsterdam crane track transforms into glass offices; a needle-thin tower stacks 28 apartments onto a 21ft-wide plot in Melbourne, Australia.</desc><category lang="en">Instructional</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19223615_b_v12_aa.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021150000 +0000" stop="20261021160000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Build That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Arctic Modules &amp; Auditoria</sub-title><desc lang="en">The engineering secrets behind a mobile research station in Antarctica, a gravity-defying concert hall on the Canary Islands, and a rotating boat lift in Scotland.</desc><category lang="en">Instructional</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19223615_b_v12_aa.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021160000 +0000" stop="20261021170000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Build That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Boxes &amp; Birds</sub-title><desc lang="en">The American Museum of Natural History in NYC gets a cave-like extension; an arts center inspired by migrating birds is built on a lake in China; Boston University gains a fossil-free, Jenga-like tower.</desc><category lang="en">Instructional</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19223615_b_v12_aa.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021170000 +0000" stop="20261021180000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Build That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Cables Cars &amp; Rooftop Parks</sub-title><desc lang="en">Witnessing amazing buildings, bridges, lifts and other structures that pushed structural concrete engineering to the edge.</desc><category lang="en">Instructional</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19223615_b_v12_aa.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021180000 +0000" stop="20261021190000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Fix That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Euro Hauler</sub-title><desc lang="en">Following a million-dollar freight run across four European countries and meeting the drivers, engineers and maintenance teams who keep the train running.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25005731_b_v8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021190000 +0000" stop="20261021200000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Fix That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Scream Machines</sub-title><desc lang="en">Mike works with repair and construction teams at Dreamworld, Australia&apos;s largest theme park, after a cyclone caused $4M in damage; they fix scream machines and finish a $50M expansion featuring the world&apos;s first triple switch rollercoaster.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25005731_b_v8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021200000 +0000" stop="20261021210000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Fix That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Toronto Tunnel</sub-title><desc lang="en">Host Mike Davidson assists on a multi-million-dollar tunnel-boring project underground in Toronto.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25005731_b_v8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021210000 +0000" stop="20261021220000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Fix That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Abandoned Oil Wells</sub-title><desc lang="en">Mike Davidson goes on a cross-country road trip to help the Well Done Foundation; they work to find and cap some of the estimated 2 million leaking, toxic abandoned oil and gas wells scattered throughout the U.S.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25005731_b_v8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021220000 +0000" stop="20261021230000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Fix That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Savannah: Mega Cranes &amp; Mega Moves</sub-title><desc lang="en">Mike helps fix the machines that keep one of the United States&apos; biggest ports moving; he assists a team in moving a 3-million pound crane.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25005731_b_v8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261021230000 +0000" stop="20261022000000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Fix That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Deep Sea Fish Farm</sub-title><desc lang="en">Host Mike Davidson helps make high-stakes repairs for one of the world&apos;s largest open-ocean fish farm operations in Panama.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25005731_b_v8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261022000000 +0000" stop="20261022010000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">How Did They Fix That?</title><sub-title lang="en">Lava Wars</sub-title><desc lang="en">In Grindavik, Iceland, crews repair earthquake fissures, build lava barriers and track magma, gases and ground movement while divers inspect a damaged harbor pier in a town shaped by ongoing eruptions.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p25005731_b_v8_ab.jpg"/></programme>
